{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>Instead of every firstborn among the children of Israel</b> – Now the firstborn were consecrated to belong to HaShem from the time He commanded, \"Sanctify to Me every firstborn among the children of Israel, of man\" etc. (Exodus 13:2), and there were many firstborn in Israel, and they had not been redeemed until now, for it had not yet been stated to whom the redemption would belong. For only now was it that the priests were consecrated, and they had not yet been commanded concerning the priestly gifts. So they stood in an undefined sanctity, and it is possible that the sacrificial service was performed by them, according to the words of our Sages (Zevaḥim 112b). And it appears to me that all these firstborn were not born in the wilderness in a single year, for the people did not multiply there to such an extent; rather, all the firstborn who were in Israel were counted, for all of them had been consecrated as I explained there (Exodus 13:11). And now He replaced them with the Levites, and they are their redemption, and He commanded that the remainder be redeemed, and He gave the redemption money to Aaron and to his sons, as it is a commandment for all generations:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:29.525158546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}